   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OECD - ATTC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OECD:s rekommendation om hantering av korruptionsrisker understryker vikten av givargemensamma svar p&#xe5; korruption. Ej koordinerade &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder anses f&#xf6;rsvaga arbetet mot korruption, och gemensamma ansatser kan uppn&#xe5;s t.ex. genom att uppmuntra givare att agera mer samst&#xe4;migt. F&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja detta tillv&#xe4;gag&#xe5;ngss&#xe4;tt kommer insatsen att bidra till en v&#xe4;gledning f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja bist&#xe5;ndspersonal i deras hantering av korruptionsfall i bist&#xe5;ndsprojekt.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The OECD Council Recommendation on Managing the Risk of Corruption explicitly refers to Joint responses to corruption. Uncoordinated actions are considered detrimental to anti-corruption efforts, and joint responses could be achieved through e.g. encouraging donors to respond collectively to the extent possible. To support this approach, the contribution will develop a set of operational guidelines, also referred to as minimum fire instructions, to assist field staff, embassies, and headquarters respectively. These are envisioned to assist in managing and responding to cases of corruption in the implementation of development co-operation projects.</narrative>
  </description>
